2025-12-01 09:55:03,305 - agent.executor - INFO - Decision: CONTINUE. Reasoning: The task needs concrete, recent data linking solar flares to geomagnetic effects and any relevance to events this week. We already confirmed numerous flares (including an X1.9 on 2025-12-01 with a 1837 km/s halo CME) and multiple CMEs, plus HSS/RBE items in late Nov. However, key gaps remain for Earth impacts around Nov 27–Dec 10: repeated connection errors blocked GST/IPS/MPC/SEP/HSS retrievals for the current week, and WSA-Enlil impact predictions didn’t show Earth yet. To finalize an evidence-backed assessment, we will: (1) re-query GST to confirm any geomagnetic storms post-2025-11-27; (2) pull GST and IPS notifications for the same window; (3) check MPC/SEP/HSS for signatures of solar wind disturbances this week; (4) update flare/CME listings after Dec 1 in case of new events; (5) re-fetch WSA-Enlil simulations spanning late Nov–early Dec for any Earth-impact modeling. These independent calls run in parallel, avoid unnecessary older data, and directly address the remaining verification needs.
