Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-29', 'end_date': '2025-12-09'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result (summarized from 1836 tokens): Coronal Mass Ejections (CMEs) found: 17 (10 detailed below; 7 additional entries referenced but not included in the excerpt)

Overall: Multiple east/NE-limb CMEs on 2025-11-29, including several fast events (up to 1932 km/s), overlapping/serial fronts around 05:48–06:48Z, and activity from/just beyond the NE limb (near N20E89) associated with C7.0 and M2.9 flares. Several events show deflection (equatorward/westward or southeast), far-sided geometry, and complex/stacked fronts.

1) ID: 2025-11-29T04:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 04:00Z; Source: S16E89
- Notes: Seen to the east in LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1. Possible source: occulted M1.5 flare from AR 14294 peaking slightly after CME start; would require significant northward deflection. Direction a bit north vs flare at S20; CME start slightly earlier than flare; part of AR may be behind limb.
- Analyses: 08:11Z, 854 km/s, Type: Cn
- Related: 2025-11-29T04:14:00-FLR-001

2) ID: 2025-11-29T04:36:00-CME-001
- Start: 04:36Z; Source: S55E40
- Notes: Visible south in LASCO C2/C3 and STEREO A; obscured by pylon in GOES CCOR-1. Possible source: faint brightening near S55E40 ~03:50Z in SUVI 195. Coronal hole N/W of source may explain southeast deflection vs measured parameters.
- Analyses: 12:16Z, 441 km/s, Type: Sn

3) ID: 2025-11-29T05:48:00-CME-001
- Start: 05:48Z; Source: not identified
- Notes: Peculiar pointy-nosed front NE in LASCO C2/C3 and NNE in STEREO A; accompanied by another directly east front and closely followed by several others (≥4 distinct fronts, best in STEREO A COR2).
- Analyses: 08:12Z, 1402 km/s, Type: On

4) ID: 2025-11-29T06:15:00-CME-001
- Start: 06:15Z; Source: not identified
- Notes: Seen east in all three coronagraphs; immediately follows the 05:48Z pointy-nosed CME. Possible source: southern lobe of a three-pronged prominence eruption from/behind the NE limb, starting ~05:36Z in SUVI 304.
- Analyses: 10:12Z, 868 km/s, Type: Cn

5) ID: 2025-11-29T06:23:00-CME-001
- Start: 06:23Z; Source: not identified
- Notes: Front directly north in STEREO A; no Earth-facing disk source → likely longitude ~−130°. Faint follow-up front after the 05:48Z CME in other coronagraphs fits this northern front at ~−130°.
- Analyses: 07:36Z, 1932 km/s, Type: On; 09:31Z, 915 km/s, Type: Cn

6) ID: 2025-11-29T06:48:00-CME-001
- Start: 06:48Z; Source: not identified
- Notes: Symmetrical ENE CME in LASCO, STEREO A, GOES; overlaps several earlier CMEs. No on-disk EUV source; fronts fit a front-sided longitude ~−73°.
- Analyses: 12:06Z, 645 km/s, Type: Cn

7) ID: 2025-11-29T09:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 09:00Z; Source: N20E89
- Notes: Fast CME east in LASCO, GOES, STEREO A. Source likely just on/beyond NE limb (N15–N25): filament ejecta from ~08:32Z (SUVI 304), field line motion (SUVI 171/195/284/304), and a C7.0 flare (SUVI 131) from an unnumbered NE-limb region. CME appears deflected equatorward and westward; triangulates near N05E79; no source observed closer to those parameters.
- Analyses: 11:48Z, 1193 km/s, Type: On
- Related: 2025-11-29T08:40:00-FLR-001

8) ID: 2025-11-29T11:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 11:00Z; Source: not identified
- Notes: East in LASCO and GOES; not seen in STEREO A despite coverage → likely on far side of STEREO A–facing disk. No corresponding Earth-facing sources; likely far-sided.
- Analyses: 16:21Z, 586 km/s, Type: Cn

9) ID: 2025-11-29T14:08:00-CME-001
- Start: 14:08Z; Source: N00E82
- Notes: Faint east CME in LASCO C3, GOES, STEREO A; missed in LASCO C2 due to downlink gap starting 13:36Z. Source may be more far-sided around east limb; only weak field line motion over AR 14294 ~14:00Z (SUVI 171/284). swpc_cat triangulation places source at N00E82 near AR 14294.
- Analyses: 17:48Z, 820 km/s, Type: Cn

10) ID: 2025-11-29T16:00:00-CME-001
- Start: 16:00Z; Source: N20E89
- Notes: East in GOES, STEREO A, LASCO. Precedes and is overlapped/collided into by a 17:00Z CME from the same region. Source: M2.9 flare from an unnumbered region just on/beyond the NE limb 
