1) ID: 2025-11-29T04:00:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43100)
- Start: 04:00Z; Source: S16E89 (possible occulted M1.5 flare from AR 14294; timing/source uncertain; likely northward deflection; part of AR behind limb)
- Seen east in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1
- Analysis: 08:11Z, 854 km/s, Type Cn
- Related: 2025-11-29T04:14:00-FLR-001

2) ID: 2025-11-29T04:36:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43140)
- Start: 04:36Z; Source: S55E40 (faint brightening ~03:50Z in GOES SUVI 195)
- Seen south in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2; obscured by pylon in GOES CCOR-1
- Coronal hole N/W of source may explain southeast deflection
- Analysis: 12:16Z, 441 km/s, Type Sn

3) ID: 2025-11-29T05:48:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43103)
- Start: 05:48Z; Source: not specified
- “Pointy-nosed” front to NE (SOHO C2/C3) and NNE (STEREO A COR2); accompanied by multiple fronts (≥4 distinct in STEREO A COR2)
- Analysis: 08:12Z, 1402 km/s, Type On

4) ID: 2025-11-29T06:15:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43105)
- Start: 06:15Z; Source: not specified
- Seen east in SOHO, STEREO A, GOES CCOR-1; immediately follows the 05:48Z CME
- Possible source: southern lobe of three-pronged prominence eruption from/behind NE limb (~05:36Z in GOES SUVI 304)
- Analysis: 10:12Z, 868 km/s, Type Cn

5) ID: 2025-11-29T06:23:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43108)
- Start: 06:23Z; Source: not specified
- Front seen directly north in STEREO A COR2; no Earth-facing source; likely longitude ~−130°
- Faint follow-up front to the 05:48Z event in other coronagraphs fits this geometry
- Analyses: 07:36Z, 1932 km/s, Type On; 09:31Z, 915 km/s, Type Cn

6) ID: 2025-11-29T06:48:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43110)
- Start: 06:48Z; Source: not specified
- Symmetrical ENE CME in SOHO, STEREO A, GOES CCOR-1; overlaps several earlier CMEs; no on-disk EUV source
- Geometry consistent with front-sided longitude ~−73°
- Analysis: 12:06Z, 645 km/s, Type Cn

7) ID: 2025-11-29T09:00:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43119)
- Start: 09:00Z; Source: N20E89 (likely just on/beyond NE limb, N15–N25)
- Fast CME to east in SOHO, GOES CCOR-1, STEREO A; filament ejecta from ~08:32Z in GOES SUVI 304; field-line motion in SUVI 171/195/284/304; C7.0 flare in SUVI 131 from unnumbered NE-limb region
- Deflected equatorward/westward; triangulation ~N05E79; no closer on-disk source
- Analysis: 11:48Z, 1193 km/s, Type On
- Related: 2025-11-29T08:40:00-FLR-001

8) ID: 2025-11-29T11:00:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43138)
- Start: 11:00Z; Source: not specified
- Seen east in SOHO LASCO C2/C3, GOES CCOR-1; not seen in STEREO A COR2 despite coverage → likely far side of STEREO A-facing disk; no Earth-facing source
- Analysis: 16:21Z, 586 km/s, Type Cn

9) ID: 2025-11-29T14:08:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43112)
- Start: 14:08Z; Source: N00E82 (per triangulation), near AR 14294
- Faint east CME in SOHO LASCO C3, GOES CCOR-1, STEREO A COR2; missed in LASCO C2 due to downlink gap from 13:36Z
- Only weak SUVI 171/284 field-line motion over AR 14294 (~14:00Z), not matching CME signature; source may be more farsided around east limb
- Analysis: 17:48Z, 820 km/s, Type Cn

10) ID: 2025-11-29T16:00:00-CME-001 (DONKI 43125)
- Start: 16:00Z; Source: N20E89
- Observed east in GOES CCOR-1, STEREO A COR2, SOHO LASCO C2/C3
