2025-12-01 10:07:40,223 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Here’s a data-backed, winter (Dec–Jan) planning snapshot for hiking and camping in California’s national parks, with current alerts, concrete numbers, and NPS sources so you can verify details.

Quick picks for early winter 2025–26 (Dec–Jan)
- Best right now for hiking + camping
  - Joshua Tree NP (jotr): Comfortable winter hiking (days around 60°F; nights near/below freezing), many front-country campgrounds, dark skies. Note two flood-related closures (details below). 7‑day vehicle fee $30. Source: NPS park page.
  - Death Valley NP (deva): Prime season for hiking; cool days/chilly nights. Some roads currently closed from Nov storms; main corridors and services still operating (gas 24h at Furnace Creek/Stovepipe Wells; Panamint Springs gas 7am–9:30pm). 7‑day vehicle fee $30. Source: NPS conditions page.
  - Pinnacles NP (pinn): Mild winter highs typically in the 60s; excellent day hiking; camping available; weekend capacity crunches possible 8am–3pm. 7‑day vehicle fee $30. Source: NPS park page and alert.

- Good with caveats
  - Channel Islands NP (chis): Spectacular winter hiking; backcountry/boat‑in camping (e.g., Anacapa) with low fees ($15/site), but access is only by concession boat/plane; some site‑specific closures. Entrance fee $0. Source: NPS park and campground pages.
  - Redwood National and State Parks (redw): Open year‑round, no entrance fee, towering forests and coastal hikes. Expect heavy winter rain (60–80 inches Oct–Apr). Special monthly “Hike & Bike Day” first Saturdays (Oct–May). Source: NPS park page and event listing.

- Snow-season parks (limited road/trail access now)
  - Yosemite NP (yose): Yosemite Valley stays open with numerous ranger programs, but Tioga Road and Glacier Point Road are closed for the season; weekday blasting closures affect access to Vernal/Nevada Falls (details below). 7‑day vehicle fee $35. Source: NPS.
  - Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs (seki): Multiple seasonal road closures (e.g., Mineral King Rd; Hwy 180 to Cedar Grove; Panoramic Point) plus a few storm-damaged spur roads closed. 7‑day vehicle fee $35. Source: NPS.
  - Lassen Volcanic NP (lavo): Main park road (Hwy 89) closed for winter; some secondary roads may be impassible after storms. Winter-discounted entry $10 (when in effect). Source: NPS alerts.

Current NPS alerts (verified; last-updated dates shown)
- Yosemite NP (yose) — https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
  - Vernal and Nevada Falls trail closures (weekday blasting for JMT repairs): No access to tops of Vernal/Nevada Falls; full Mist Trail closed during blasting; JMT closed between Clark Point and Panorama Trail junction; Panorama Trail near JMT junction closed. Only access to Vernal Fall footbridge and Clark Point. Last updated 2025‑11‑26. Info: nps.gov#wilderness (via alert) and road conditions page below.
  - Tioga Road (Hwy 120 through the park) and Glacier Point Road: Temporarily closed due to snow. Last updated 2025‑11‑21. Road conditions: 209‑372‑0200 then 1, 1. More: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm

- Redwood N&SP (redw) — https://www.nps.gov/redw/index.htm
  - Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway closed to vehicles Dec 1–3 for maintenance; open to pedestrians and bicyclists. Last updated 2025‑11‑24.

- Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs (seki) — https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
  - Winter seasonal road closures: Mineral King Rd; Hwy 180 between Grant Grove and Cedar Grove; Panoramic Point Rd. Last updated 2025‑11‑23. Details: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm
  - A few small roads closed due to damage: Middle Fork Rd; Redwood Canyon Rd; South Fork Rd; Crystal Cave Rd. Last updated 2025‑09‑11.

- Joshua Tree NP (jotr) — https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
  - Queen Valley Complex roads closed due to flooding (Bighorn Sheep Rd, Queen Valley Rd, O’dell Rd). Last updated 2025‑11‑16.
  - Oasis of Mara Trail closed due to heavy flooding until further notice. Last updated 2025‑09‑28.
  - Caution: Some third‑party hiking apps have inaccurate info; use official NPS app. Last updated 2024‑03‑11. Info: https://www.nps.gov/subjects/digital/nps-apps.htm

- Death Valley NP (deva) — https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
  - Many roads closed due to flooding from Nov 15/18 storms; open roads can have water/debris/equipment. Drive cautiously. Last updated 2025‑11‑19. Conditions: https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm
  - Gas pumps at Panamint Springs Resort closed at night; open 7am–9:30pm daily. Gas at Furnace Creek and Stovepipe Wells is 24 hours. Last updated 2025‑01‑27.

- Lassen Volcanic NP (lavo) — https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
  - Lassen National Park Highway (Hwy 89) closed for winter at the SW and NW gates. Last updated 2025‑11‑17.
  - Roads to Butte Lake, Juniper Lake, Warner Valley may be impassible after storms. Last updated 2025‑11‑19.
  - Burned-area hazards persist from the 2021 Dixie Fire (obey closures). Last updated 2024‑08‑26. Burned area safety: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/burned-area-safety.htm

- Channel Islands NP (chis) — https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm
  - Santa Rosa Island: Temporary closure of China Camp and Cluster Point beaches/dunes to protect sensitive resources; travel only on marked paths. Last updated 2024‑02‑22. Details: https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/backcountry-beach-camping-on-santa-rosa-island.htm
  - Santa Barbara Island dock closed (landings restricted to adjacent rocky ledge). Last updated 2018‑01‑23. Conditions: https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/conditions.htm

- Pinnacles NP (pinn) — https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
  - High crowds & park capacity: When lots fill (commonly 8am–3pm weekends), traffic holds at the campground until space is available. Last updated 2022‑01‑19. Hours: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm

Upcoming ranger programs and events (Dec 1, 2025–Jan 15, 2026)
- Yosemite Valley (Yosemite NP)
  - Family Ranger Talk: Daily through Jan 27, 2026 (All day listing; check at Yosemite Valley Welcome Center). Host: NPS.
  - Guided Nature Walk: Daily through Jan 27, 2026 (Yosemite Valley Lodge Amphitheater). Host: Yosemite Hospitality.
  - Yosemite After Dark: Night nature walk, daily through Jan 27 (bring flashlight).
  - Evening Programs at Yosemite Valley Lodge Cliff Room: Multiple dates in Dec and Jan.
  - Discovery Walk (easy ranger walk): Select Tue–Wed dates in Dec and Jan.
  - The Ahwahnee Historic Hotel Tour: Complimentary 1‑hour tour, daily through Jan 27. Source: NPS events listing embedded in park feed.

- Redwood N&SP
  - Forest Walk: Prairie Creek (family-friendly, ~1 mile): Weekends from Dec 6, 2025 to May 3, 2026 starting at Prairie Creek Visitor Center (41.363822, -124.023154).
  - Hike and Bike Day: Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway (10 mi scenic drive closed to vehicles; e‑bikes allowed up to 20 mph): First Saturdays Oct–May. Next date in this window: Sat Dec 6, 2025. Access/parking details in event text above. Source: NPS events feed.

- Channel Islands NP
  - Guided Hikes on the Islands: Offered on days concessioner boats run; hikes and times announced during island orientation. Dates listed many days from 2025‑12‑01 forward. Source: NPS events feed.

Camping options with specific numbers, seasons, and fees (examples to get you started)
- Joshua Tree NP
  - Belle Campground: 18 sites; first‑come, first‑served (FCFS); $25/night (Senior/Access $12.50). Vault toilets; no water; RVs up to 35 ft; max per site: 6 people, 3 tents, 2 cars if space. Source: NPS campground data.
  - Many other campgrounds exist; due to popularity, FCFS sites can fill—arrive early, especially weekends. Official NPS app is recommended for updates.

- Death Valley NP
  - Multiple campgrounds operated by NPS and concessioners; winter is peak camping season. Check active road/campground status due to Nov flooding before you go: https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/conditions.htm

- Pinnacles NP
  - Front‑country camping available near the East Entrance (campground details on NPS site). Expect weekend capacity controls 8am–3pm when parking fills. Hours and alerts: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm

- Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs (winter caveat: several roads closed)
  - Azalea Campground (Grant Grove area, elev. 6,500 ft): 110 sites. Open year‑round. Nov–Apr: about 20 sites FCFS with cashless payment via Recreation.gov app; May–Oct: all sites by reservation (up to 4 months ahead). Fee $32/night (Senior/Access $16). RVs to 47 ft; trailers to 30 ft. ADA site 30. Source: NPS campground data. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10124502
  - Atwell Mill (Mineral King; elev. ~6,650 ft): 21 tent‑only sites; typically late May–late Oct. Reservations required; book up to 1 month in advance. Fee $32/night (Senior/Access $16). Source: NPS campground data. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10044710
  - Road access note: Mineral King Rd is closed for winter; see SEKI road conditions: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm

- Lassen Volcanic NP (winter access is limited)
  - Backcountry camping: Permit required for all overnight trips. Fees: $6 admin per permit + $5 per person per trip (no per‑night fee). Bear‑resistant containers required Apr 16–Nov 30. Source: NPS. Permit: https://www.recreation.gov/permits/4675334
  - Butte Lake Campground (remote, elev. ~6,100 ft): 101 sites; reservations required during operating season (up to 6 months ahead). Standard fee $22 (or $15 when water off). RVs/trailers to 35 ft; group and stock sites available. Seasonal operations; check current status. Source: NPS. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234156

- Redwood National and State Parks
  - No NPS entrance fee; car/RV campgrounds here are operated by California State Parks. NPS‑led programs/events continue year‑round. Expect rain; dress for wet conditions. Source: NPS park page.

- Channel Islands NP (boat/plane access only)
  - Anacapa Island Campground: 7 primitive, walk‑in tent sites (½ mile from landing + 157 stairs); $15/site/night; open year‑round; no water; pit toilets, picnic table, food locker. Reservations required via Recreation.gov (or 877‑444‑6777). Western gull nesting Apr–mid‑Aug brings rookery conditions; bring extra supplies in case boats can’t dock due to weather. Source: NPS campground page. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232502
  - Check island‑specific closures (e.g., Santa Rosa beach/dune closure; Santa Barbara dock status): https://www.nps.gov/chis/planyourvisit/conditions.htm

Entrance fees (7‑day, unless noted)
- Yosemite NP: Private vehicle $35; motorcycle $30; per‑person $20; annual Yosemite pass $70. Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs: Private vehicle $35; motorcycle $30; per‑person $20; annual SEKI/Hume Lake pass $70. Source: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Joshua Tree NP: Private vehicle $30; motorcycle $25; per‑person $15; annual park pass $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Death Valley NP: Private vehicle $30; motorcycle $25; per‑person $15; annual park pass $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
- Lassen Volcanic NP: Private vehicle $30 (winter‑discounted $10 when applicable); motorcycle $25 (winter $10); per‑person $15 (winter $10); annual 4‑park regional pass $55 (Lassen, Crater Lake, Whiskeytown, Lava Beds). Source: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Pinnacles NP: Private vehicle $30; motorcycle $25; per‑person $15; annual park pass $55. Source: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Redwood N&SP: No entrance fee. Source: https://www.nps.gov/redw/index.htm
- Channel Islands NP: No entrance fee (boat/plane fares separate). Source: https://www.nps.gov/chis/index.htm

Seasonal/weather facts to plan by
- Joshua Tree: Winter days around 60°F (15°C); nights can be at or below freezing; generally clear, <25% humidity. Source: NPS park page.
- Death Valley: Winter has cool days, chilly nights; rare rain; snow on high peaks. Source: NPS park page.
- Pinnacles: Mediterranean; winter highs typically in the 60s; cold nights; big day–night swings inland. Source: NPS park page.
- Yosemite: Most of park snow‑covered Nov–May; Valley can see rain or snow in storms; eastern Tioga Pass entrance typically closes approx. Nov to late May/June. Source: NPS park page.
- Sequoia & Kings Canyon: Snow in giant sequoia groves in winter; chains may be required. Source: NPS park page.
- Lassen: Average January temp ~40.4°F high / 20.8°F low; the park highway closes for winter and snow can exceed 30 ft annually. Source: NPS park page.
- Redwood: Coastal temps mid‑40s to mid‑60s year‑round; Oct–Apr rainfall about 60–80 inches; dress for rain and mud. Source: NPS park page.

