- Rules: See laws/policies: http://www.nps.gov/chis/learn/management/lawsandpolicies.htm
- Weather info: http://channelislands.noaa.gov/news/kiosk.html
- Contact: 805-658-5730; chis_information@nps.gov
- Location: Anacapa Island, CA 93001 (34.0143426535, -119.367763068)

Backcountry Camping in Lassen’s Wilderness (Lassen Volcanic NP, CA – parkCode: lavo)
- Type: Backcountry only; no designated sites/amenities.
- Permit: Required for all overnight backcountry stays; obtain online only at recreation.gov (https://www.recreation.gov/permits/4675334). One permit per trip; group size max 10; carry a copy (digital/print). No in-person/mail/email requests.
- Fees: $6 nonrefundable administrative fee per permit, plus $5 per person per trip (no per-night fee).
- Operating: Year-round; winter access limited by deep snow; when main park road is closed, camping allowed on/near the road.
- Key regulations: Max stay 30 days/year; some areas closed near developed areas, water bodies, hydrothermal features (see full list: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/learn/management/backcountryregulations.htm). Bear-resistant containers required Apr 16–Nov 30. Pets not allowed; no bicycles; no hunting; firearms only with valid CA CCW. No overnight stock use. Pack out all trash; catholes for human waste; pack out TP/hygiene. Vehicles may be left overnight in parking areas per permit.
- Weather: Little precip July–Sept; up to 40 ft snow in winter; snow can linger into July/Aug; weather varies with elevation—be prepared.
- Accessibility: No ADA trails/facilities; uneven primitive conditions; OPDMDs not allowed in wilderness.
- Contact: lavo_information@nps.gov
- Location: 38050 Highway 36 E, Mineral, CA 96063 (40.4995725567, -121.3462823681)

Butte Lake Campground (Lassen Volcanic NP, CA – parkCode: lavo)
- Location: NE corner of park; 6-mile Butte Lake Road (off Hwy 44); ~45 min from NW Entrance/Manzanita Lake; elevation ~6,100 ft; remote.
- Reservations: Required for all sites entire season; up to 6 months ahead (best to reserve before arrival; connectivity in park is limited). Hosts/staff do not handle reservations. 9/3–10/14: only Loop B open and water off (no drinking water/flush toilets). Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234156
- Fees: Campsite $22; $15 when water off (early/late season). Group site $62; $35 when water off. Stock corral $37.
- Sites: Total 101 (reservable listed 107); 6 group; 1 horse/corral; RVs/trailers allowed up to 35 ft. ADA: Site A-6.
- Amenities: Seasonal potable water; seasonal vault toilets; no showers; dump station; camp store; host onsite; food storage lockers.
- Regulations: Leashed pets; drones prohibited; must occupy site upon payment; stays limited to 14 days/year; checkout 12 pm; quiet hours 10 pm–6 am; generators 8–10 am, 12–2 pm, 5–7 pm. Wash dishes at campsite only. Dead/down wood collection limited (within 30 ft of road; <4" diameter); no chainsaws. Fires only in provided grates; no rock rings; fully extinguish.
- Weather: Typical highs 68–84°F; lows 29–39°F; usually snow-free by June; snow may linger on peaks into July/Aug.
- Contact: 530-595-6121; lavo_fees@nps.gov
