Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3057 tokens): - Name: Yosemite National Park (code: yose)
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Description: Iconic Sierra Nevada park (nearly 1,200 sq mi) renowned for waterfalls, deep valleys, meadows, ancient giant sequoias, vast wilderness, and granite formations. First protected in 1864.
- Location: Latitude 37.84883288, Longitude -119.5571873
  - Address: PO Box 577, Yosemite National Park, CA 95389
- Contacts:
  - Phone (Voice): 209/372-0200
  - Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Weather
- Elevation range: ~2,000–13,000 ft (600–4,000 m).
- Precipitation: ~95% falls Oct–May (over 75% Nov–Mar).
- Snow: Most of park snow-covered Nov–May; Yosemite Valley can have rain or snow during winter storms.

Directions
- Year-round vehicle access via Highways 41, 140, and 120 from the west.
- Tioga Pass Entrance (Highway 120 from the east) typically closed approx. Nov through late May/June.
- Hetch Hetchy open year-round but may close intermittently due to snow.
- Note: GPS directions may be inaccurate within/near the park.
- More info: http://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/driving.htm

Operating Hours
- Yosemite National Park: Open 24 hours/day, 365 days/year.
- Hetch Hetchy: Open sunrise to sunset for day visitors; all day visitors must exit by sunset. Road closed sunset to sunrise to all vehicles (including backpackers without appropriate permits).

Entrance Fees
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $35. Valid 7 consecutive days; covers vehicle and all occupants (non-commercial car, pickup, RV, or van ≤15 seats).
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $30. Valid 7 consecutive days (per motorcycle).
- Entrance – Per Person: $20. Valid 7 consecutive days for entry on foot, bicycle, horse, or non-commercial bus/van. Age 15 and younger free.
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan: $25 + $20 per person, not to exceed $105. Valid 7 days. Commercial Use Authorization (CUA) required.
- Commercial Entrance – Van: $125. Valid 7 days. CUA required.
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus: $200. Valid 7 days. CUA required.
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach: $300. Valid 7 days. CUA required.
- Entrance – Non-commercial Groups: $20 per person up to a maximum of $300 per vehicle. Age 15 and younger free.
- Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0 with approved educational fee waiver (accredited or tax-exempt groups on trips for educational/scientific purposes related to Yosemite; not primarily recreational).
- Commercial Entrance – Per Person: $20. Also described as $25 plus $20 per person, not to exceed $105; valid 7 days. CUA required.

Entrance Passes
- Annual Entrance – Park: $70. Free entrance to Yosemite for 12 months from purchase date.

