Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'lavo'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3193 tokens): Lassen Volcanic National Park (code: lavo)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Description: Home to steaming fumaroles, wildflower meadows, clear mountain lakes, and numerous volcanoes. Jagged peaks reflect an eruptive past; hot water continues shaping the landscape.

Weather
- Highly variable. Average January temps: high 40.4 °F (4.7 °C), low 20.8 °F (-6.2 °C). Average July temps: high 88.4 °F, low 49.8 °F. On average: 36.9 days ≥ 90 °F and 164 days ≤ 32 °F annually.

Directions
- From I-5 (Redding): Hwy 44 east 48 mi to Hwy 89; south 1 mi to north entrance.
- From I-5 (Red Bluff): Hwy 36 E 51 mi to Hwy 89; north 6 mi to south entrance.
- Directions page: http://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Location
- Coordinates: 40.49354575, -121.4075993
- Address: 38050 Highway 36 East, Park Headquarters, Mineral, CA 96063

Contacts
- Phone (Voice): 530 595 6100
- Email: lavo_information@nps.gov

Entrance Fees (valid up to 7 consecutive days; when booths unstaffed, buy digital passes at recreation.gov)
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $30.00
- Entrance – Private Vehicle (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $25.00
- Entrance – Motorcycle (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Per Person (foot/bike; also non-commercial organized group in one vehicle): $15.00
- Entrance – Per Person (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0.00 (fee waiver application required ≥2 weeks prior)
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan: $25.00
- Commercial Entrance – Van: $50.00
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus: $60.00
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach: $150.00
  Note: Commercial tour = packaged/priced/sold itinerary for leisure/recreation by an organization that realizes financial gain; fees based on total seating capacity regardless of passenger count; annual/lifetime passes not accepted.

Entrance Passes
- Annual Entrance – Park: $55.00. Valid for one year from month of purchase at four NPS units: Lassen Volcanic NP, Crater Lake NP, Whiskeytown NRA, Lava Beds NM. Admits one vehicle and all occupants, or one motorcycle and riders, or pass holder + 3 others on bicycle/foot.

Operating Hours
- Entire park, all entrances: Open year-round. Road access is limited approx. November–May due to snow.
- Standard hours: Monday–Sunday: All Day.

Topics
- Arts; Explorers and Expeditions; Native American Heritage; Science, Technology and Innovation; Wars and Conflicts; Colonial/European Contact Conflicts; Westward Expansion; Women’s History
- Natural resources/features: Animals; Birds; Cats (wild); Fish; Climate Change; Fire; Forests and Woodlands; Coniferous Forests; Geology; Groundwater; Freshwater Springs; Geothermal; Hot Springs; Grasslands; Meadows; Lakes; Mountains; Natural Sounds; Night Sky; Astronomy; Rock Landscapes and Features; Scenic Views; Trails; Unique Species; Rare; Volcanoes; Watersheds; Waterfalls; Wilderness

Activities
