Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2983 tokens): Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Description: Volcanic eruptions ~23 million years ago formed today’s dramatic rocky spires, canyons, and diverse habitats ranging from chaparral and oak woodlands to cool, shaded canyon floors.

Location
- Coordinates: 36.49029208, -121.1813607
- Address: 5000 East Entrance Road, Paicines, CA 95043

Weather
- Mediterranean climate: hot, dry summers; mild winters with moderate precipitation.
- Inland location yields greater seasonal and day–night temperature swings.
- Summer highs can exceed 100°F; winter highs typically in the 60s.

Getting There
- West entrance: via Hwy 101 → City of Soledad → Hwy 146.
- East entrance: via Hwy 25 (from Hollister in the north; from King City via Bitter Water Road G-13 in the south).
- Important: No through road between east and west entrances.
- Directions: http://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Contacts
- Phone (Voice): 831-389-4486
- Fax: 831-389-4288
- Email: pinn_visitor_information@nps.gov (include visit dates/season; typical reply within 1 week). For volunteering: pinn_volunteer@nps.gov

Entrance Fees (valid 1–7 days unless noted)
- Private Vehicle: $30. Includes all occupants; valid at East and West Entrances.
- Motorcycle: $25. Includes all riders; valid at East and West Entrances.
- Per Person (on foot/bike): $15.
- Non-commercial Groups (16+ passenger capacity): $15 per person, up to commercial group maximums ($40 or $100). Exempt: age 15 and under, anyone with applicable pass, and hired drivers.
- Commercial Entrance:
  - Sedan (1–6 seats): $30
  - Van (7–15 seats): $40
  - Mini-bus (16–25 seats): $40
  - Motor Coach (26+ seats): $100
  - Applies to packaged/priced/sold leisure itineraries; fee based on seating capacity, not passenger count; ages/passes don’t affect price.
- Education/Academic Groups: $0 with approved Educational Fee Waiver (otherwise, see large/commercial group fees).

Entrance Passes
- Pinnacles Annual Pass: $55. Valid 12 months from month of purchase; covers pass signee and accompanying passengers in one non-commercial vehicle. Available at entrance stations.

Operating Hours
- East Side Entrance: Open 24/7, year-round (including holidays).
- West Side Entrance: Daily 7:30 AM–8:00 PM. One-lane, narrow, winding road; oversize vehicles should use the east side. Access to Prewett Point, Balconies, and Juniper Canyon trails.

Activities
- Astronomy and stargazing
- Biking (road)
- Camping (car/front country, group, RV)
- Caving
- Rock climbing
- Picnicking
- Citizen science, volunteer vacation
- Hiking (front country, backcountry)
- Junior Ranger Program
- Wildlife watching and birdwatching
- Park film
- Shopping (bookstore, gift shop/souvenirs)

Topics (highlights)
- History and culture: architecture/building, archeology, colonization/settlement, missions, immigration/migrations, Latino/Hispanic and Native American heritage, military/US Army, presidents, schools/education, industry/mining, ranches/farming/agriculture, transportation (roads, bridges, tunnels), social movements (conservation), Westward Expansion (homesteading, Gold Rush), Great Depression.
- Natural features and processes: volcanoes, geology, fossils/paleontology, caves/karst, canyons, mountains, rock formations, grasslands/meadows, forests (coniferous/deciduous), shrublands, foothills/valleys, rivers/riparian, wetlands, waterfalls, watersheds/headwaters, groundwater/aquifers/springs, climate change, fire, night sky/natural sounds, scenic views, trails, wilderness.
- Wildlife: birds, fish, tortoises/turtles, wild cats, wolves; unique, rare, endangered species.
- Tragic events: floods, catastrophic fires.
- Wars/conflicts: Spanish-American War, Cold War.
- Science, technology, engineering (including dams).

