Source: https://nginx.org/en/docs/njs/reference

This method adds data (which can be a string or Buffer) to a chain of chunks designated for forwarding. Data can be sent to a client (in a download callback) or to an upstream server (in an upload callback). An optional `options` object allows overriding Nginx buffer flags, such as `last` or `flush`.

```javascript
s.send(data[, options])
```

