What’s the latest stable you can use right now (with evidence)
- On NixOS 25.11 (current stable channel), nginx is packaged as version 1.28.0.
  - Evidence (NixOS package index, channel 25.11): search result shows nginx 1.28.0; detailed package info confirms 1.28.0
    - https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=25.11&show=nginx
    - Tool evidence: nixos_info(name=nginx, channel=25.11) → Version: 1.28.0
- On Nixpkgs “unstable” channel, nginx is also currently 1.28.0 (so both stable and unstable channels are aligned at the moment).
  - Evidence: nixos_info(name=nginx, channel=unstable) → Version: 1.28.0
- Nixpkgs version history confirms the most recent bump to 1.28.0 on 2025‑11‑23 with commit ee09932cedcef15aaf476f9343d1dea2cb77e261.
  - Evidence: https://nixhub.io/packages/nginx (shows 1.28.0 last updated 2025‑11‑23 21:50 UTC; commit ee09932cedcef15aaf476f9343d1dea2cb77e261)

Which line (stable vs mainline) to choose
- Upstream NGINX historically distinguishes “stable” vs “mainline” and recommends mainline for most users.
  - You can verify this on the official download page (shows “mainline version” and “stable version”): https://nginx.org/en/download.html and in the docs: https://nginx.org/en/docs/
- NixOS module documentation echoes this recommendation:
  - services.nginx.package description: “This defaults to the stable version. Note that the nginx team recommends to use the mainline version which [is] available in nixpkgs as nginxMainline.” (Default: pkgs.nginxStable)
  - Evidence: https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.package
- Practical takeaway: If you want the most up-to-date features (e.g., recent HTTP/3/QUIC improvements), use mainline; for maximum conservatism, use the NixOS default. In current 25.11, nginx resolves to 1.28.0 either way.

Official documentation (primary sources)
- NGINX main documentation index: https://nginx.org/en/docs/
- NGINX Download page (lists mainline and stable with version numbers): https://nginx.org/en/download.html
- NGINX Beginner’s Guide (good starting point): https://nginx.org/en/docs/beginners_guide.html
- NGINX Admin Guide and modules: linked from https://nginx.org/en/docs/

NixOS integration (system-level) you can rely on
- Enable and package selection:
  - services.nginx.enable (boolean; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.enable
  - services.nginx.package (package; default pkgs.nginxStable; see note on mainline): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.package
- Declarative vhosts:
  - services.nginx.virtualHosts (attrset submodule; default includes localhost): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.virtualHosts
  - Example in docs shows enableACME and forceSSL usage.
- “Recommended” one‑liners that simplify setup:
  - services.nginx.recommendedProxySettings (bool; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedProxySettings
  - services.nginx.recommendedGzipSettings (bool; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedGzipSettings
  - services.nginx.recommendedBrotliSettings (bool; default false; auto-adds pkgs.nginxModules.brotli): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedBrotliSettings
  - services.nginx.recommendedTlsSettings (bool; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedTlsSettings
  - services.nginx.recommendedOptimisation (bool; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedOptimisation
  - services.nginx.recommendedUwsgiSettings (bool; default false): https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.recommendedUwsgiSettings

Home Manager options
- There is no dedicated Home Manager module for nginx.
  - Evidence: “No Home Manager options found matching ‘nginx’.”
- Implication:
  - On NixOS: manage nginx via the system module (services.nginx.*).
  - On non-NixOS using Home Manager: you can manage config files under $HOME (home.file.*), but you cannot run system nginx as a user service via HM alone. You’d use your OS’s service manager or containers.

Minimal NixOS example to get started (uses the “recommended” presets)
- Add something like this to configuration.nix:
  - services.nginx.enable = true;
  - services.nginx.recommendedProxySettings = true;
  - services.nginx.recommendedGzipSettings = true;
  - services.nginx.recommendedBrotliSettings = true;
  - services.nginx.recommendedTlsSettings = true;
  - services.nginx.virtualHosts."example.local" = {
      forceSSL = true;
      enableACME = true;
      locations."/" = { proxyPass = "http://127.0.0.1:3000"; };
    };
- You can verify each option in the NixOS options links above. The defaults for the recommended* settings are false; setting them to true applies sane presets without hand‑coding each directive.

Summary
- Concrete version packaged in NixOS 25.11 stable: nginx 1.28.0 (same in unstable at time of checking). Verified in the NixOS package index and nixos_info; NixHub shows last update 2025‑11‑23 (commit ee09932…).
- Upstream recommends mainline; NixOS module defaults to a “stable” build but acknowledges upstream guidance. If you need the newest features, switch to mainline; otherwise keep the default.
- Home Manager does not have an nginx module; use NixOS services.nginx or manage files manually if you’re not on NixOS.

Sources (verifiable)
- NixOS package index (25.11): https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=25.11&show=nginx
- NixOS unstable package info: https://search.nixos.org/packages?channel=unstable&show=nginx
- NixHub version history for nginx (shows 1.28.0, commit ee09932…): https://nixhub.io/packages/nginx
- NixOS options:
  - services.nginx.enable: https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.enable
  - services.nginx.package: https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.package
  - services.nginx.virtualHosts: https://search.nixos.org/options?channel=25.11&show=services.nginx.virtualHosts
  - recommended* toggles: Proxy/Gzip/Brotli/TLS/Optimisation/Uwsgi (links above)
- Official NGINX docs:
  - Docs index: https://nginx.org/en/docs/
  - Download (shows current mainline and stable numbers): https://nginx.org/en/download.html
  - Beginner’s Guide: https://nginx.org/en/docs/beginners_guide.html

