- services.nginx.appendConfig (strings, concatenated with “\n”): Lines appended to generated nginx.conf. Can be set multiple times; values concatenate. Commonly used by modules providing http snippets. Unlike config, which can be set only once.
- services.nginx.appendHttpConfig (strings): Lines appended to the generated http block. Mutually exclusive with using config and httpConfig to specify the whole http block verbatim.
- services.nginx.clientMaxBodySize (string): Sets global client_max_body_size.
- services.nginx.commonHttpConfig (strings): Common http context definitions (e.g., log_format, resolver) placed before use in server/location.
- services.nginx.config (string): Verbatim nginx.conf. Mutually exclusive with other nginx.conf options except appendConfig, httpConfig, and logError. For additional verbatim config alongside other options, use appendConfig.
- services.nginx.defaultHTTPListenPort (uint16): Default HTTP port if vhosts don’t specify listen.port.
- services.nginx.defaultListen (list of submodules): Default listen entries for vhosts; takes precedence over defaultListenAddresses and other listen defaults.
  - .addr (string): IP address.
  - .extraParameters (list of strings): Extra listen parameters.
  - .port (null or uint16): Port number.
  - .proxyProtocol (bool): Enable PROXY protocol.
  - .ssl (null or bool): Enable SSL.
- services.nginx.defaultListenAddresses (list of strings): Default listenAddresses for vhosts. Equivalent to defaultListen = [ { addr = "0.0.0.0"; } ].
- services.nginx.defaultMimeTypes (absolute path): Default MIME types (from mailcap, more complete than upstream defaults).
- services.nginx.defaultSSLListenPort (uint16): Default SSL port if vhosts don’t specify listen.port.
- services.nginx.enable (bool): Enable Nginx web server.
- services.nginx.enableQuicBPF (bool): Enable QUIC packet routing via eBPF to support connection migration. Requires Linux 5.7+. Grants extended capabilities (CAP_SYS_ADMIN, CAP_NET_ADMIN).
- services.nginx.enableReload (bool): Reload nginx when the config file changes instead of restart. Config exposed at /etc/nginx/nginx.conf. See systemd.services.*.restartIfChanged.
- services.nginx.eventsConfig (strings): Lines inside the events block.
- services.nginx.experimentalZstdSettings (bool): Enable alpha‑quality zstd module with recommended settings; adds pkgs.nginxModules.zstd to additionalModules.
- services.nginx.gitweb.enable (bool): Enable gitweb integration.
- services.nginx.gitweb.group (string): Group for the CGI process (use config.services.gitolite.group if using gitolite).
- services.nginx.gitweb.location (string): Path location to serve gitweb.
- services.nginx.gitweb.user (string): User for the CGI process.
- services.nginx.gitweb.virtualHost (string): VirtualHost for gitweb (default is catch‑all).
- services.nginx.group (string): Group account under which nginx runs.
- services.nginx.httpConfig (strings): Lines inside the http block. Mutually exclusive with structured configuration via virtualHosts and the recommended*Settings options. Use appendHttpConfig to append to the generated http block.
- services.nginx.logError (string): Error logging. First param is destination (file path, “stderr”, or “syslog:” prefix for syslog). Second param is level: debug, info, notice, warn, error, crit, alert, emerg. Default level: error. Setting a level logs that and all more severe levels.
- services.nginx.mapHashBucketSize (null or positive int): Bucket size for map variables hash tables. Default depends on CPU cache line size; see nginx docs on hashes.
- services.nginx.mapHashMaxSize (null or positive int): Max size for map variables hash tables.
- services.nginx.package (package): Nginx package to use. Defaults to stable; upstream recommends mainline (nixpkgs: nginxMainline). Supported forks: angie, openresty, tengine.
