Tool `Context7:get-library-docs` with Parameter {'context7CompatibleLibraryID': '/websites/nginx_en', 'topic': 'download', 'tokens': 4000} on Context7 succeeded. Result (summarized from 11157 tokens): Summary of key points

Nginx stream (njs) session APIs
- s.send(data[, options]): Queue data (string or Buffer) for forwarding to client (download) or upstream (upload). options can set Nginx buffer flags like last, flush.
- s.on(event, callback): Register callback for stream events: upload, download, upstream, downstream. Callback gets (data, flags), where flags.last indicates last buffer.
- s.allow(): Alias for s.done(0); finalize current phase successfully and continue processing.

Nginx stream proxy rate limiting
- proxy_download_rate 0: Default is 0 (disabled).
- Use variables to limit download rate per connection:
  - map $slow $rate { 1 4k; 2 8k; }
  - proxy_download_rate $rate;

Nginx HTTP rewrite
- rewrite regex replacement [flag]: Rewrites URI using regex and replacement. Flags: last, break, redirect, permanent.
- Example mapping media paths:
  - rewrite ^(/download/.*)/media/(.*)\..*$ $1/mp3/$2.mp3 last;
  - rewrite ^(/download/.*)/audio/(.*)\..*$ $1/mp3/$2.ra last;

uWSGI byte-range handling
- uwsgi_force_ranges off; Controls byte-range support for uWSGI responses regardless of Accept-Ranges header; useful for clients needing partial content.

OIDC
- userinfo off; Default disables downloading UserInfo data.

HLS playlist generation
- GET /{media_file}.m3u8 with optional query parameters:
  - start, end (seconds; since 1.9.0), offset (positive from start, negative from end; since 1.9.0), len (target fragment length).
- Returns an M3U8 playlist (application/x-mpegURL).

njs/Node.js filesystem APIs (sync unless noted)
- readlinkSync(path[, options]): Return target of symlink; encoding string/object; buffer encoding returns Buffer.
- statSync(path[, options]): Return fs.Stats; option throwIfNoEntry (default true) controls exception vs undefined.
- filehandle.stat(): Async; Promise resolving to fs.Stats.
- symlinkSync(target, path): Create symlink; returns undefined on success.
- realpathSync(path[, options]): Resolve canonical absolute path; encoding string/object.
- unlinkSync(path): Delete file; undefined on success.
- renameSync(oldPath, newPath): Move/rename; undefined on success.
- rmdirSync(path): Remove directory; undefined on success.
- readSync(fd, buffer, offset[, length[, position]]): Read into buffer; returns bytesRead.
- writeSync(fd, string[, position[, encoding]]): Write string; returns bytesWritten.
- writeFileSync(filename, data[, options]): Write or replace file content; options mode, flag.
- Examples:
  - Synchronously read a file: const buf = fs.readFileSync('/path.tar.gz'); buf.slice(0,2).toString('hex') -> '1f8b'.
  - Asynchronously read: fs.promises.readFile('/file/path').then(data => { ... });

WebCrypto objects and APIs (njs)
- CryptoKey: Read-only properties: algorithm, extractable, type (secret|private|public), usages (encrypt|decrypt|sign|verify|deriveKey|deriveBits).
- CryptoKeyPair: { privateKey: CryptoKey, publicKey: CryptoKey }.
- crypto.subtle.verify(algorithm, key, signature, data): Verify signature; algorithm forms:
  - RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5: "RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5" or { name }
  - RSA-PSS: { name: "RSA-PSS", saltLength }
  - ECDSA: { name: "ECDSA", hash: "SHA-256"|"SHA-384"|"SHA-512" }
  - HMAC: "HMAC" or { name }
  - Returns Promise<boolean>.

njs Response object
- new Response(body?, { headers?, status?, statusText? }): Create HTTP response object.

Protobuf.js and bundling for njs
- Install and generate static module (njs cannot do dynamic class generation):
  - npm install protobufjs
  - npx pbjs -t static-module helloworld.proto > static.js
- Bundle with Browserify (include source maps with -d):
  - npx browserify load.js -o bundle.js -d
- Validate bundle:
  - node ./njs_bundle.js
  - njs ./njs_bundle.js
  - njs ./njs_bundle.js | hexdump -C

