Tool `Context7:get-library-docs` with Parameter {'context7CompatibleLibraryID': '/websites/nginx_en', 'topic': 'versioning', 'tokens': 2000} on Context7 succeeded. Result (summarized from 11772 tokens): Summary of key NGINX and njs information

njs (JavaScript for NGINX)
- Request info: r.httpVersion is a read-only property with the client’s HTTP protocol version for the current request.
- Global njs object:
  - Properties: version (e.g., "0.7.4"), version_number (numeric hex, e.g., 0x000704), memoryStats.size (bytes claimed).
  - Methods: njs.dump(value) pretty-prints; njs.on('exit', callback) registers VM exit handler.
- CLI usage: njs can execute expressions (echo "2**3" | njs -q → 8) and exposes globalThis with njs/process/env details.
- Module loading and scripts:
  - Obsolete: js_include http.js with js_content version returning njs.version; prefer js_import.
  - js_preload_object map.json loads an immutable JSON object named map at configure time.
- Node modules and bundling for njs:
  - Browserify: npx browserify load.js -o bundle.js -d (source maps).
  - Webpack/Babel: npx webpack --config webpack.config.js (outputs e.g., dist/wp_out.js).
  - Protobuf.js: npm install protobufjs; npx pbjs -t static-module helloworld.proto > static.js. Expose as global.hello via load.js (global.hello = require('./static.js')). Final bundled code uses global.hello for serialization and a setbuf wrapper.
- TypeScript definitions: git clone https://github.com/nginx/njs; cd njs && ./configure && make ts → build/ts/{njs_core, njs_shell, ngx_http_js_module, ngx_stream_js_module}.d.ts.
- Deprecated string-to-bytes helpers: toUTF8()/toBytes(); use Buffer instead.
- Filesystem APIs:
  - renameSync(oldPath, newPath): sync rename/move; returns undefined or throws.
  - realpathSync(path[, options]): canonical path resolution; returns string.
  - symlinkSync(target, path): create symlink; returns undefined or throws.

NGINX HTTP API (ngx_http_api_module)
- GET /api/: lists supported API versions. Example response: { "versions": ["9","8","7","6","5","4","3","2"] }.
- GET /api/{version}/nginx: returns NGINX config/status for a specific version; fields query param filters output (e.g., version, build).
- GET /nginx: status of the running instance (version, build, address, reloads, master/worker PIDs); fields optional; 404 UnknownVersion possible.
- Example general info JSON (similar to API output): includes version, build, address, generation, load_timestamp, timestamp, pid, ppid.
- Example API requests (v9): /api/9/, /api/9/nginx, /api/9/connections, /api/9/workers, /api/9/http/requests, server_zones, caches, upstreams, keyvals, stream equivalents.
- Status module examples: /status, /status/nginx_version, /status/caches/cache_backend, /status/upstreams[/backend[/peers/1[/weight]]], and stream equivalents.

Key directives and defaults
- proxy_http_version 1.0 (default; 1.1 enables keepalive and features; since 1.1.4).
- server_tokens on (default; includes version on error pages and Server header).
- proxy_cache_revalidate off (since 1.5.7); on → conditional origin checks (If-Modified-Since/If-None-Match).
- proxy_next_upstream_timeout 0 (disables time limit; since 1.7.5).
- ssl_certificate_cache off (since 1.27.4).
- ssl_certificate_compression off (TLS 1.3 cert compression; OpenSSL 3.2+; since 1.29.1).
- grpc_ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3 (default protocols since 1.23.4).
- ssl_ecdh_curve auto (default; pre-1.11.0 was prime256v1).
- Obsolete ssl directive: ssl off; deprecated 1.15.0, removed 1.25.1. Use listen ... ssl.

NGINX Stream and SSL features
- Route by TLS version: map $ssl_preread_protocol $upstream to steer clients (e.g., SSH vs TLSv1.2) with ssl_preread on; can multiplex SSH/HTTPS on same port.
- proxy_requests 0 (default; since 1.15.7).
- Proxy client certificates/keys:
  - proxy_ssl_certificate file (variables allowed since 1.21.0).
  - proxy_ssl_certificate_key file or store:scheme:id via OpenSSL provider (since 1.29.0); variables allowed since 1.21.0.
- Listen on port ranges: listen 127.0.0.1:12345-12399; listen 12345-12399 (since 1.15.10).
- Upstream load balancing: random [two method] (since 1.15.1).

