2025-12-01 10:38:22,993 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Here’s a concise, source-backed plan to explore near Golden Gate Park (GGP) with minimal travel time, rain-safe options, and verified operating info where available. I combined: (1) live weather (WeatherAPI via our Weather Data tool), (2) National Park Service (NPS) official data for nearby federal sites (alerts, hours, locations), and (3) map-based proximity estimates from the Music Concourse area inside GGP for practical walking choices. Notes on data provenance and any estimates are clearly labeled.

What’s verified right now (weather and official alerts)
- Current conditions (San Francisco, last updated 2025-12-01 02:15 local): Partly cloudy; 4.4°C (39.9°F), feels like 3.0°C (37.4°F), humidity 97%, wind 6.1 kph ENE, visibility 14 km, UV 0.0. Source: WeatherAPI via tool.
- 3-day forecast (San Francisco):
  - 2025-12-01: Max 13.3°C / 55.9°F, Min 6.5°C / 43.7°F, “Cloudy,” chance of rain 0%, max wind 13.3 kph, avg humidity 85%. Source: WeatherAPI via tool.
  - 2025-12-02: Max 11.1°C / 52.0°F, Min 8.9°C / 48.0°F, “Partly Cloudy,” chance of rain 0%, max wind 12.2 kph, avg humidity 92%. Source: WeatherAPI via tool.
  - 2025-12-03: Max 16.4°C / 61.5°F, Min 8.8°C / 47.8°F, “Partly Cloudy,” chance of rain 0%, max wind 13.7 kph, avg humidity 67%. Source: WeatherAPI via tool.
  - Practical takeaway: next few days show 0% rain probability in the forecast; it’s cool and humid, so bring layers. Re-check the morning of your visit.

- Relevant NPS alerts (Golden Gate National Recreation Area, which includes Lands End, Fort Point, Presidio areas near GGP). Sources: nps.gov feeds via tool.
  - 2025-12-02 (approx. 8 AM–4 PM) Bunker Road lot closure (east end of Baker-Barry Tunnel). If you were considering Marin Headlands that day, plan alternate parking. Last updated 2025-11-25. Source: NPS goga alerts.
  - Fort Mason upper roads/parking closures (Fall 2025–Fall 2026) for projects; watch signage, towing enforced. Last updated 2025-11-03. Source: NPS goga alerts.
  - Caution: marine mammals (leptospirosis spike) – keep dogs leashed; report stranded animals to The Marine Mammal Center 415-289-7325. Source + details: https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/nature/wildlife-viewing-guidelines.htm
  - Auto-theft caution at overlooks/parking: remove valuables, lock doors. Source: https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/news/larceny-from-autos-at-ggnra.htm

Walkable attractions starting from the Music Concourse (keep travel short, pick indoor if rain threatens)
Important: The Google Maps API blocked live distance calls, so the walk times below are practical estimates based on straight-line distances and typical park paths, starting near the California Academy of Sciences/de Young. Verify your exact route in Google/Apple Maps day‑of.

- California Academy of Sciences (indoors; planetarium, rainforest dome, aquarium)
  - Location: on the Music Concourse. Walking: ~0–0.1 km (2–3 min).
  - Good rainy-day anchor stop.

- de Young Museum (indoors; art + Hamon Observation Tower when open)
  - Location: opposite side of the Music Concourse. Walking: ~0.2 km (3–5 min).

- Japanese Tea Garden (mostly outdoors, partially sheltered)
  - Location: just south of de Young. Walking: ~0.2–0.3 km (3–5 min).

- San Francisco Botanical Garden (outdoors; many paths have some canopy)
  - Main gate at 9th Ave & Lincoln Way. Walking: ~0.8 km (10–15 min).

- Conservatory of Flowers (indoors; warm greenhouses—excellent if cold)
  - East on JFK Dr. Walking: ~1.0 km (12–15 min).

- Stow Lake + Boathouse (outdoors; boats are weather/conditions dependent)
  - Walking: ~1.3 km (about 18–20 min) to the boathouse.

- Haight–Ashbury (shops/cafés; weather-safe interlude)
  - Walking: ~1.8 km (about 22–25 min) to Haight & Ashbury.

Short hops beyond the park (official hours verified via NPS)
- Lands End Lookout Visitor Center (indoor exhibits on Sutro Baths/Lands End)
  - Hours: Daily 9:00 AM–5:00 PM. Location: 680 Point Lobos Ave, San Francisco, CA 94121. Coordinates: 37.779730, -122.511612. Source: NPS visitor center listing via tool.
  - From Music Concourse: ~5.0 km walking (about 70–80 min); faster via transit/rideshare. Best on clear days.

- Fort Point National Historic Site (beneath Golden Gate Bridge; partially indoors)
  - Typical hours: 10:00 AM–5:00 PM with seasonal open days (often Fri–Sun fall–spring; 5 days/week in many summers). Check current status here: https://www.nps.gov/fopo/index.htm
  - Address: Building 999, Marine Drive, San Francisco, CA 94129; Coordinates: 37.808374, -122.473747. Source: NPS park page via tool.

- Golden Gate Bridge Welcome Center (indoor exhibits/gift shop)
  - Hours: Daily 9:00 AM–6:00 PM (may vary). Location: Golden Gate Bridge Plaza, SF 94129. Phone: 415-426-5220. Source: Parks Conservancy center listing via NPS visitor centers feed.

- Presidio Visitor Center (good indoor orientation stop if you head north)
  - Hours: Daily 10:00 AM–5:00 PM (closed Thanksgiving, Christmas, New Year’s Day). Address: 210 Lincoln Blvd, SF 94129. Coordinates: 37.801941, -122.456850. Phone: 415-561-4323. Source: NPS prsf visitor center via tool.

How to use the weather to optimize your day
- If drizzle/cold picks up: Do a fully “indoors-first” loop inside GGP to minimize exposure:
  1) California Academy of Sciences → 2–3 min walk →
  2) de Young Museum → 3–5 min walk →
  3) Conservatory of Flowers (12–15 min walk).
- If skies hold (forecast shows 0% rain for 12/1–12/3): Add short outdoor segments:
  - Japanese Tea Garden (+5 min from de Young), Botanical Garden (+10–15 min), Stow Lake loop (+18–20 min).
- If it turns clear and you want ocean views:
  - Lands End (Visitor Center open 9–5) and Sutro Baths are great; consider a quick rideshare or bus to cut travel time.

Key verifiable details and sources (for quick checking)
- Weather (current + 3-day): WeatherAPI dataset via tool (San Francisco, CA). Last updated 2025-12-01 02:15. Values listed above.
- NPS alerts (closures/hazards): Golden Gate National Recreation Area (park code: goga) alert feed via tool:
  - Bunker Road lot closure 2025-12-02 (8 AM–4 PM).
  - Fort Mason roads/parking closures (Fall 2025–Fall 2026).
  - Marine mammal/leptospirosis caution: https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/nature/wildlife-viewing-guidelines.htm
  - Auto-theft caution: https://www.nps.gov/goga/learn/news/larceny-from-autos-at-ggnra.htm
- NPS visitor centers/hours near GGP:
  - Lands End Lookout VC: hours 9–5; coordinates 37.779730, -122.511612. Source: NPS via tool.
  - Presidio Visitor Center: hours 10–5 daily; 210 Lincoln Blvd. Source: NPS via tool: https://www.nps.gov/prsf/planyourvisit/presidio-visitor-center.htm
  - Fort Point NHS (hours vary seasonally; typical 10–5): https://www.nps.gov/fopo/index.htm
  - Golden Gate Bridge Welcome Center (9–6): https://www.parksconservancy.org/services/golden-gate-bridge-welcome-center (listed in NPS feed)

Notes and limitations
- Live Google Maps distance/time calls were blocked during this run (403/geocode errors), so walk times above are practical estimates from the Music Concourse. Please verify your exact walking/transit route in Google/Apple Maps on the day you go.
- GGP institutions (California Academy of Sciences, de Young, Conservatory of Flowers, SF Botanical Garden, Japanese Tea Garden) are not managed by NPS; for latest hours/tickets, check their official sites before you go:
  - California Academy of Sciences: https://www.calacademy.org/
  - de Young Museum: https://deyoung.famsf.org/
  - Conservatory of Flowers: https://conservatoryofflowers.org/
  - SF Botanical Garden: https://www.sfbotanicalgarden.org/
  - Japanese Tea Garden: https://japaneseteagardensf.com/

Quick, low-risk half-day plan you can share
- Rain-safe 3–4 hours: California Academy of Sciences (indoors) → de Young (indoors) → lunch/coffee at Music Concourse → Conservatory of Flowers (indoors). All walks 2–15 minutes each.
- Clear-sky 3–5 hours: de Young → Japanese Tea Garden → Botanical Garden → Stow Lake loop. If energy/time remains, rideshare to Lands End Lookout (open 9–5) for Sutro Baths overlook.

