Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'goga'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3048 tokens): Golden Gate National Recreation Area (code: goga)
- Designation: National Recreation Area
- State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/goga/index.htm
- Overview: A vast urban park spanning 60+ miles of mostly coastal lands north and south of San Francisco, supporting 19 ecosystems and 2,000+ plant and animal species. Offers hiking, vistas, picnicking, and deep history across Indigenous cultures, Spanish colonialism, the Mexican Republic, US military expansion, and San Francisco’s growth.

Location
- Coordinates: 37.85982543, -122.6007386
- Headquarters address: Golden Gate National Recreation Area, 201 Fort Mason, San Francisco, CA 94123

Weather
- Winter: Sporadic rain, cool; grass greens.
- Late Feb–May/June: Blooming trees/flowers.
- July: Summer fog predominates along the coast; grasses/plants turn golden brown/muted grays through summer/fall.
- Sept–Oct: Clear skies and abundant sunshine park-wide.

Getting There
- Access via Highways 1, 101, 280 (from north/south Bay Area) and Highway 80 (from the East Bay).
- Park HQ at Fort Mason: enter at Franklin and Bay Streets, San Francisco.
- Directions: http://www.nps.gov/goga/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Contacts
- Phone: 415-561-4700
- Email: goga_socialmedia_goga@nps.gov

Entrance Fees/Passes
- No park-wide entrance fees or passes listed here; site-specific fees may apply—check individual site pages.

Operating Hours
- Parking Lots: Most areas of the urban park are accessible 24/7, but most parking lots are open sunrise to sunset.
- Day Use Areas: Open 6:00 a.m. to 1 hour after sunset.
  - Marin County: Conzelman Rd (west, between traffic circle and Field Rd.), Kirby Cove (except registered campers), Muir Beach, Muir Beach Overlook, Stinson Beach.
  - San Francisco County: Fort Point (north of the gate and adjacent areas), China Beach, Fort Mason – Black Point Stairway to Van Ness Ave., Lands End, Sutro Heights Park.
- Muir Woods National Monument: Open daily; hours vary seasonally. Check the Muir Woods website for current information (availability may vary with public health guidance).
- Point Bonita Lighthouse (beyond the tunnel): Open Mon, Fri, Sat, Sun 12:30 pm–3:30 pm; closed Tue–Thu.
- Nike Missile Site (Marin Headlands): Open Thu–Sat 12:00 pm–3:00 pm for demonstrations/programs (unless otherwise posted).
- Battery Townsley: Open first Sunday of each month, 12:00 pm–4:00 pm for guided tours.
- Fort Point National Historic Site: Open Fri–Sun 10:00 am–5:00 pm (check Fort Point’s website for updates).

Activities
- Arts and Culture; Museum Exhibits; Living History/Reenactments; Junior Ranger Program; Shopping (Bookstore/Park Store).
- Hiking (front-country), Biking (including mountain biking).
- Camping (front-country/car, group).
- Horseback riding/trekking.
- Guided tours; self-guided walking tours.
- Picnicking; Dining.
- Fishing (saltwater).
- Surfing.
- Wildlife watching/Birdwatching.

Themes and Topics (highlights)
- History and culture: Native American heritage; Spanish missions/colonization; Mexican Republic; US military history (Army, Coast Guard; forts, coastal defenses, artillery, infantry, cavalry); Civil War, Spanish-American War, WWI, WWII, Vietnam, Cold War; Alcatraz/incarceration; Japanese-American internment; immigration and urban America; bridges and maritime history (lighthouses, shipwrecks); cemeteries/monuments; religion/spirituality; social movements (abolition, civil rights, conservation); women’s, African American, Hispanic/Latino, Asian American, LGB American heritage; Gold Rush; westward expansion; explorers/expeditions; industry and logging; medicine/hospitals; tragic events (fires, forced marches).
- Nature and science: Coasts, islands, dunes, estuaries, wetlands/marshes; watersheds; oceans/whales; forests (including coniferous), grasslands/prairies, foothills/valleys; geology; climate change; fire; unique/rare/endangered species; natural sounds; scenic views; trails; animals (birds, fish, turtles).
- Built environment: Architecture and buildings


