7) What to say in your conclusions
- Today’s top open LLMs are Qwen2.5, Llama 3.x, Gemma 3, Mistral/Mixtral, Phi-3.x, and DeepSeek-R1 distillations. Evidence: strong reported scores (Qwen2 paper) alongside very high adoption on Hugging Face.
- Gains come from better data and targeted post-training: trillion-scale, high-quality, deduplicated web corpora (FineWeb/Dolma/RefinedWeb) and carefully constructed instruction/preference datasets (OASST1, UltraChat, HH-RLHF, UltraFeedback).
- Reasoning is being pushed by RL-style training (DeepSeek-R1) and “verify-then-select” paradigms (e.g., GSM8K verifier approaches), while serving is getting faster via speculative decoding.
- Evaluation is shifting to harder, more robust tests (MMLU-Pro, GPQA) and long-context suites (LongBench).

