- Qwen: Qwen/Qwen-7B-Chat

Paper summary (verbatim essence):
- Models must have world knowledge and problem-solving ability to do well.
- Best available (then) large-scale model (GPT-3) exceeds random accuracy by ~20 points on average but is still far from expert level on every task.
- Models show uneven strengths, poor self-assessment, and near-random performance on important areas like morality and law.
- The benchmark enables comprehensive evaluation across many domains and highlights key deficiencies.
