Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2309.00071'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 104471 tokens): Title: YaRN: Efficient Context Window Extension of Large Language Models

Authors: Bowen Peng, Jeffrey Quesnelle, Honglu Fan, Enrico Shippole

Problem: Transformer LLMs using Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE) do not generalize well beyond the sequence lengths seen in training.

Contribution (YaRN):
- Proposes YaRN (Yet another RoPE extensioN), a compute-efficient method to extend context windows of RoPE-based LLMs.
- Training efficiency: requires 10x fewer tokens and 2.5x fewer training steps than prior context-extension methods.
- Performance: enables LLaMA models to effectively use and extrapolate to much longer contexts than in pre-training, surpassing prior state of the art for context window extension.
- Generalization: can extrapolate beyond the limited context of the fine-tuning dataset.

Released checkpoints:
- Llama 2 7B and 13B fine-tuned with YaRN for 64k and 128k context windows.
- Code/checkpoints: https://github.com/jquesnelle/yarn

Paper page: https://huggingface.co/papers/2309.00071
arXiv ID: (not provided in the content)

Implementations and related models (selection/highlights):
- Direct/explicit:
  - NousResearch/Yarn-Mistral-7b-128k (Mistral 7B adapted with YaRN; 128k context)
  - Llama 2 7B/13B (64k/128k) via the authors’ YaRN repo above
- Broad adoption/tagging indicates widespread relevance across long-context and Qwen-family models (many tagged with arxiv:2309.00071), including:
  - Qwen series: Qwen2 / Qwen2.5 / Qwen3 and derivatives across sizes (e.g., 3B–235B; base and instruct; coder and VL variants) such as:
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B/14B/32B/72B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B/14B/32B(-Instruct)
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B/7B/32B/72B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen3-4B/8B/14B/30B-A3B, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-235B-A22B, and “Next”/MoE variants
    - Qwen/QwQ-32B (and quantized formats: GGUF, AWQ)
  - GradientAI long-context Llama 3 variants:
    - gradientai/Llama-3-8B-Instruct-262k
    - gradientai/Llama-3-8B-Instruct-Gradient-1048k
  - Tongyi-Zhiwen/QwenLong-L1-32B (long-context reasoning model)
  - Unsloth GGUF ports for Qwen3 MoE (e.g., unsloth/Qwen3-30B-A3B-GGUF)

Key takeaways:
- YaRN makes long-context extension of RoPE-based LLMs substantially cheaper while improving extrapolation.
- Demonstrated state-of-the-art context extension on LLaMA and evidence of extrapolation beyond fine-tuning limits.
- Publicly available long-context Llama 2 checkpoints (64k/128k) and a growing ecosystem of models referencing or adopting YaRN-like long-context techniques.
