Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2407.13833'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 168893 tokens): Title: Phi-3 Safety Post-Training: Aligning Language Models with a “Break-Fix” Cycle

Authors: Emman Haider; Daniel Perez-Becker; Thomas Portet; Piyush Madan; Amit Garg; David Majercak; Wen Wen; Dongwoo Kim; Ziyi Yang; Jianwen Zhang; Hiteshi Sharma; Blake Bullwinkel; Martin Pouliot; Amanda Minnich; Shiven Chawla; Solianna Herrera; Shahed Warreth; Maggie Engler; Gary Lopez; Nina Chikanov; Raja Sekhar Rao Dheekonda; Bolor-Erdene Jagdagdorj; Roman Lutz; Richard Lundeen; Tori Westerhoff; Pete Bryan; Christian Seifert; Ram Shankar Siva Kumar; Andrew Berkley; Alex Kessler

Problem and motivation
- Small, high-performing language models that can run on-device (e.g., smartphones) are increasingly deployed across domains.
- Ensuring these models are aligned with human preferences and safety requirements is critical.

Core contribution
- Presents a safety alignment methodology for the Phi-3 series using an iterative “break-fix” cycle.
- Cycle components: repeated rounds of (1) dataset curation, (2) safety post-training, (3) benchmarking, (4) red teaming, and (5) vulnerability identification.
- Coverage spans a variety of harm areas in both single- and multi-turn interactions.

Findings
- Iterative break-fix post-training led to consistent improvements for Phi-3 models across a wide range of responsible AI benchmarks.

Link
- Paper page: https://huggingface.co/papers/2407.13833

