Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2502.12404'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 99908 tokens): Title: WMT24++: Expanding the Language Coverage of WMT24 to 55 Languages & Dialects
Link: https://huggingface.co/papers/2502.12404 (arXiv:2502.12404)

Authors: Daniel Deutsch, Eleftheria Briakou, Isaac Caswell, Mara Finkelstein, Rebecca Galor, Juraj Juraska, Geza Kovacs, Alison Lui, Ricardo Rei, Jason Riesa, Shruti Rijhwani, Parker Riley, Elizabeth Salesky, Firas Trabelsi, Stephanie Winkler, Biao Zhang, Markus Freitag

What this work does:
- Extends the WMT24 machine translation (MT) dataset to 55 languages by adding 46 new languages/dialects.
- Provides new human-written references and post-edits for the 46 additions.
- Adds post-edits of references for 8 of the 9 original WMT24 languages.
- Covers four domains: literary, news, social, and speech.
- Benchmarks a variety of commercial MT providers and LLMs on the new dataset using automatic metrics.
- Finds that LLMs are the best-performing MT systems in all 55 languages on automatic evaluation.
- Notes that results should be confirmed with human evaluation in future work.

Key points:
- Scope: 55 languages total (46 new languages/dialects beyond WMT24).
- Annotations: human-written references + post-edits for new languages; post-edits for 8/9 original WMT24 languages.
- Domains: literary, news, social, speech.
- Evaluation: automatic metrics (human evaluation left for future work).
- Outcome: LLMs outperform other MT systems across all covered languages.

