- Current NPS alerts/closures
  - Mist Trail/John Muir Trail blasting closures near Vernal/Nevada Falls (weekdays); only Vernal Fall footbridge and Clark Point accessible; no access to tops of Vernal/Nevada Falls when blasting occurs. Last updated: 2025‑11‑26. Source: NPS Yosemite alerts feed.
  - Tioga Road (Hwy 120 through the park) and Glacier Point Road closed for the season due to snow. Last updated: 2025‑11‑21. Road conditions line 209‑372‑0200 (then 1, 1). More: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm
- Visitor center
  - Big Oak Flat Information Station (near Big Oak Flat Entrance on Hwy 120): typically late May–early Oct, daily 8:00a–5:00p. Source: NPS Yosemite visitor centers listing.
- Weather (Yosemite Valley, CA)
  - Current (last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15): 46.9°F (8.3°C), mostly cloudy; wind NE 4.5 mph; humidity 80%.
  - 3‑day forecast highs/lows: 12/1 59/39°F (sunny), 12/2 58/44°F (sunny), 12/3 58/35°F (sunny). Source: WeatherAPI feed for “Yosemite Valley, CA.”
- Events (Dec–Jan)
  - Daily ranger and partner programs in Yosemite Valley (Family Ranger Talk; Guided Nature Walk; Yosemite After Dark), plus The Ansel Adams Gallery photography walks and smartphone photo classes. Date ranges: 2025‑12‑01 to 2026‑01‑27 (specific dates vary by program). Source: NPS Yosemite events: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/calendar.htm (events retrieved for 2025‑12‑01 to 2026‑01‑31).
- Campgrounds (examples)
  - Camp 4: open year‑round; $10 per person/night; 61 tent‑only walk‑in sites; reservations required in peak season (Apr–Nov, typically 1 week ahead), otherwise self‑register; no RVs/trailers. Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/camp4.htm and NPS campgrounds feed.
  - Bridalveil Creek: typically mid‑July–early Sept; ~115 sites; $36/site/night; elevation 7,200 ft; reservations required (released 14 days ahead). Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/bvcamp.htm
- Entrance fees
  - $35/vehicle (7 days), $30/motorcycle, $20/person; Yosemite Annual Pass $70. Source: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/fees.htm

SEQUOIA & KINGS CANYON NATIONAL PARKS (SEKI) (park code: seki)
- Current NPS alerts/closures
  - Winter seasonal road closures in effect: Mineral King Road; CA‑180 between Grant Grove and Cedar Grove; Panoramic Point Road. Last updated: 2025‑11‑23. More: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm
  - Additional closures from roadway damage: Middle Fork, Redwood Canyon, South Fork, and Crystal Cave Roads. Last updated: 2025‑09‑11. Source same as above.
