Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'jotr'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2037 tokens): Joshua Tree National Park (code: jotr)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Description: Where the Mojave and Colorado deserts meet, featuring diverse plants and animals shaped by strong winds and occasional rain. Notable for dark night skies, rich cultural history, surreal geology, and vast Southern California wilderness.

Weather
- Generally clear, <25% humidity.
- Spring/Fall: comfortable; avg highs ~85°F (29°C), lows ~50°F (10°C).
- Winter: cooler days ~60°F (15°C), freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations.
- Summer: hot; days >100°F (38°C), nights often >75°F (24°C).

Directions
- From I-10: Exit 117 to CA Hwy 62 for West Entrance, North Entrance, Black Rock, and Indian Cove.
- From I-10: Exit 168 for the South Entrance.
- Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/directions.htm

