- Website: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Description: Formed by volcanic eruptions ~23 million years ago, the park features rocky spires, deep canyons, chaparral, oak woodlands, and cool, shaded canyon floors.

Weather
- Mediterranean climate; hot, dry summers and mild, wetter winters.
- Inland from the Pacific; wide seasonal and day–night temperature swings.
- Summer highs can exceed 100°F; winter highs typically in the 60s.

