  - Services: Information desk, wilderness permits, Yosemite Conservancy bookstore. Winter: self-registration permits (Crane Flat & Tioga Road trailheads) on porch; bring bear canister when closed. Accessible parking in front.
  - Hours: Open approx late May–early Oct, daily 8:00am–5:00pm.
  - Contact: 209-372-0200; yose_web_manager@nps.gov.

- Black Rock Nature Center (Joshua Tree NP, parkCode: jotr)
  - Location: In Black Rock Campground. From Hwy 62, turn south on Joshua Lane or Avalon Ave ~5 miles.
  - Address: 9800 Black Rock Canyon Rd, Yucca Valley, CA 92284.
  - Services: Bookstore, art gallery/exhibits, ranger info, picnic area, water-bottle fill, restrooms (flush).
  - Hours: Typically daily 8:00–11:00am & 12:00–4:00pm (closed 11–12; may vary). Summer (from June 1): Thu–Sun 9:00am–4:00pm; Mon–Wed closed.
  - Contact: 760-367-5500; jotr_info@nps.gov.

- Cedar Grove Visitor Center (Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs, parkCode: seki)
  - Location: Cedar Grove, ~30 mi east of Grant Grove on CA-180; next to Sentinel Campground; historic cabin by South Fork Kings River (elev. 4,600 ft).
  - Address: Northside Drive, Kings Canyon NP, CA 93633.
  - Services: Park info, maps, brochures; potable water; accessible restrooms; nearby ranger-led program venues.
  - Hours: Seasonal (late spring–mid-Sept typical); may be closed weekdays early/late season; may close for lunch anytime. Typical daily 9:00am–5:00pm.
  - Contact: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov.

- Channel Islands National Park Visitor Center (parkCode: chis)
  - Location: Robert J. Lagomarsino VC, Ventura Harbor, Ventura, CA.
  - Address: 1901 Spinnaker Dr, Ventura, CA 93001.
  - Services: Bookstore, marine life displays, island exhibits, 25-min film “A Treasure in the Sea” (CC on request). Fully accessible.
  - Hours: Daily 8:30am–5:00pm; closed Thanksgiving & Dec 25.
  - Contact: 805-658-5730; fax 805-658-5799; chis_information@nps.gov.

- Cottonwood Visitor Center (Joshua Tree NP, parkCode: jotr)
  - Location: Pinto Basin Rd, ~7 mi north of I-10 Exit 168 (South Entrance).
  - Services: Exhibits, bookstore, maps, entrance passes, water fill, ranger info; restrooms (flush toilets currently out of service).
  - Hours: Year-round, daily 8:30am–4:00pm.
  - Contact: 760-367-5500; jotr_info@nps.gov.

- Crescent City Information Center (Redwood NP/State Parks, parkCode: redw)
  - Location: Bottom floor of park HQ; corner of 2nd & K Sts, downtown Crescent City.
  - Address: 1111 2nd St, Crescent City, CA 95531.
  - Services: Information, picnic area, retail sales.
  - Hours: Summer daily 9:00am–5:00pm; Winter daily 9:00am–4:00pm.
  - Contact: (707) 464-6101; redw_information@nps.gov.

- Foothills Visitor Center (Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs, parkCode: seki)
  - Location: Generals Hwy, 1 mi east of Ash Mountain Entrance.
  - Address: 47050 Generals Hwy, Three Rivers, CA 93271.
  - Services: Info, maps, books/gifts, water, restrooms; exhibits on foothills ecology & human history. Self-issue wilderness permits (non‑quota season) at Wilderness Office behind VC.
  - Hours: Year-round except weather/emergency/operational closures; hours vary; typical daily 8:00am–5:00pm.
  - Contact: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov.

