Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose,seki,redw,jotr,deva,pinn,chis,lavo', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 138276 tokens): Summary of provided campground/backcountry info (key details)

Anacapa Island Campground (Channel Islands NP, parkCode: chis)
- Location: Anacapa Island, CA 93001; 34.0143426535, -119.367763068. Distance from landing: 0.5 mi with 157-stair climb.
- Season/Hours: Open year-round.
- Sites/Types: 7 primitive, tent-only, walk/boat-to; all reservable.
- Fees: $15/site/night. For 6 sites fee covers up to 4 people; 1 site covers up to 6. No park entrance fee.
- Reservations: Required via Recreation.gov (https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232502) or 877-444-6777. Info: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/anacapa-island/r/campgroundDetails.do?contractCode=NRSO&parkId=70984
- Amenities: Picnic tables, food storage lockers, vault toilets; no water. Bring extra day of supplies in case boat pickup is delayed.
- Weather: No shade; wind/sun exposure; fog any season; current: http://channelislands.noaa.gov/news/kiosk.html
- Regulations/Warnings: Western gull nesting Apr–mid-Aug (guano, odor, noise, carcasses; protective birds). Regulations: http://www.nps.gov/chis/learn/management/lawsandpolicies.htm
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs/limited mobility; no roads; RVs/trailers not allowed.
- Contact: 805-658-5730; chis_information@nps.gov

Atwell Mill Campground (Sequoia NP, parkCode: seki)
- Location: Mile 19.1, Mineral King Rd, Sequoia NP, CA 93271; 36.46466811749612, -118.6696721882438; along East Fork Kaweah River. Limited services at Silver City Resort (1.7 mi E); more in Three Rivers (23 mi W; ~1.5 hrs).
- Season/Hours: Usually late May–late Oct; potable water not always available in spring/fall. All reservations only; can book up to 1 month in advance.
- Sites/Types: 21 tent-only; all reservable.
- Fees: $32/site/night (up to 6 people). Senior/Access Pass: $16/site/night (excludes group sites).
- Reservations: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10044710; info: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/atwell.htm
- Amenities: Vault toilets (seasonal), trash, potable water (seasonal). No showers, dump station, store (in park listing, general amenities not specifically available here).
- Weather/Elevation: 6,650 ft; be prepared for three-season camping even in summer.
- Regulations: Black bears active—use metal food boxes; pets allowed in campground on leash ≤6 ft; no pets on park trails. Pet info: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/pets.htm; Campground regs: https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cg_regs.htm
- Accessibility/Access: Unpaved, rutted/uneven roads; no accessible sites currently; unpaved road access OK in good weather. No RVs/trailers allowed.
- Contact: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov

Azalea Campground (Kings Canyon NP, parkCode: seki)
- Location: Azalea Drive, Grant Grove, CA 93633; 36.741334350936064, -118.96777677768745. Centrally located; elevation 6,500 ft.
- Season/Hours: Open year-round. Winter (Nov–Apr): one loop with 20 sites, first-come, first-served. Summer (approx. May–Oct): reservations only; can book up to 4 months in advance (initial 20 sites in early Jan, ~90 more two weeks later). Gates open/close at 12 pm on open/close dates. Check-in after 12 pm; check-out before 12 pm.
- Sites/Types: 110 total; all reservable in summer. RVs/trailers allowed (max RV 47 ft; trailer 30 ft). Site 30 is designated accessible (level, tent pad, extended table, raised fire ring; connects via flat, paved road).
- Fees: $32/site/night (up to 6). Senior/Access: $16/site/night. Winter payments cashless via Recreation.gov mobile app QR scan; download app before arrival.
- Reservations/Info: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10124502; https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/azalea.htm
- Amenities: Flush toilets (year-round), potable water (year-round), trash, dump station nearby (per general amenities list), no showers.
- Weather: Warm/sunny summers but variable; prepare for three-season camping; winters cold/snowy.
- Regulations: Bear food storage required; pets 
