Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 44101 tokens): Summary of provided Yosemite campgrounds data (partial list; dataset indicates total 15):

General
- Weather: Yosemite (2,000–13,000 ft) gets ~95% of precipitation Oct–May (75% Nov–Mar). Snow covers most of the park Nov–May; Valley may be rainy/snowy in winter storms. Check forecast: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/weathermap.htm
- Bears/food storage: Required at all campgrounds. Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/bears.htm and https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/lockers.htm
- Regulations overview: Pets rules vary; wood/charcoal fires generally permitted with seasonal time limits in Yosemite Valley; max 6 people per site (group sites differ); max 2 vehicles per site, must fit on pads; trailers not counted if they fit. Full regs: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/campregs.htm

Bridalveil Creek Campground (parkCode: yose)
- Location/elevation: Along Glacier Point Road near Bridalveil Creek; 7,200 ft; 7 miles W of Glacier Point, 9 miles E of Wawona Road turnoff; ~45 minutes from Yosemite Valley; no services nearby. Coords: 37.6636576344, -119.624293366. Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/bvcamp.htm
- Season/reservations: Typically mid-July–early Sept; reservations required for all sites (incl. 3 horse, 2 group). Released 14 days before arrival at 7 am PT; high competition. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232453
- Fees/night: $36 (non-group); $75 (group); $50 (stock/horse).
- Sites: total 115; reservable 116; FCFS 0. Types: group 2; horse 3; tent-only 41; electrical hookups 0; RV-only 0; walk/boat-to 0; other 69.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; seasonal flush toilets; potable water (seasonal); no showers; cell reception; laundry; amphitheater; dump station; camp store; host onsite; ice/firewood sales; food lockers; internet connectivity.
- Accessibility/vehicles: No designated accessible sites. RVs allowed (max 35 ft); trailers allowed (max 24 ft); paved access roads. ADA info: no designated accessible sites.
- Key regs: Pets permitted (not in group sites). Wood/charcoal fires permitted. Max 6 people/site (group: 13–30). Max 2 motor vehicles/site (must be on pad; trailers don’t count if they fit). Contact campground office for overflow parking details.
- Contact: 209/375-9535; yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Camp 4 Campground (parkCode: yose)
- Location/elevation: Yosemite Valley near base of granite cliffs close to Yosemite Falls; 4,000 ft; near shuttle; near services at Yosemite Valley Lodge and Yosemite Village. Coords: 37.7420541116, -119.602253055. Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/camp4.htm
- Season/reservations: Open year-round. In 2025, Apr 18–Nov 15: reservations required, available 1 week in advance; remaining season FCFS with self-registration; space assigned per person in shared campsites (up to 6 per site); ranger may assist. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10004152
- Fees/night: $10 per person.
- Sites: total 61; reservable 0; FCFS 25. Types: tent-only 61; walk/boat-to 61; no RVs/trailers allowed.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; year-round flush toilets; potable water (year-round); no showers; cell reception; laundry; amphitheater; dump station; camp store; host onsite; ice/firewood sales; food lockers; internet connectivity.
- Accessibility/vehicles: 2 accessible sites; accessible parking/path; accessible restrooms; remainder has rough dirt access routes. No RVs/trailers. ADA details as above.
- Key regs: Pets not permitted. Wood fires allowed year-round; in Yosemite Valley May–Sept, campfires only 5–10 pm (charcoal any time); air quality may be unhealthy at night. Max 6 people/site. Food storage required.
- Contact: 209/372-8502; yose_web_manager@nps.gov

