Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'seki', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 44118 tokens): Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (SEKI) – campground highlights and key details

Park-wide regulations and contacts
- Wildlife and food storage: Black bears are active. Store all food and scented items in provided metal lockers. More info: nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/bears.htm
- Pets: Allowed in campgrounds/leashed (max 6 ft); not allowed on any park trails (including in backpacks). More info: nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/pets.htm
- Typical gate/check times (where specified): Gates open/close at noon on opening/closing dates. Check-in noon or later; check-out before noon.
- General contact: 559-565-3341 (voice), 559-565-3730 (fax); SEKI_Information@nps.gov. Group campground inquiries may use SEKI_Interpretation@nps.gov.

Atwell Mill Campground (Sequoia NP)
- Season/elevation: Typically late May–late Oct; 6,650 ft. Weather can change quickly; plan for three-season camping.
- Location/services: Along East Fork of the Kaweah River; Mineral King Rd mile 19.1; limited services at Silver City Resort (1.7 mi E); fuller services in Three Rivers (23 mi W; ~1.5 hrs).
- Reservations: All sites reservation-only; typically open in April; book up to 1 month in advance.
- Sites/vehicles: 21 sites; tent-only. No RVs/trailers. Roads unpaved/rutted/uneven.
- Fees: $32/night; $16/night with Senior/Access Pass.
- Water/toilets: Potable water seasonal; vault toilets (seasonal).
- Accessibility: No designated accessible sites yet; parks plan to create them.
- Links: Info nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/atwell.htm; Reserve recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10044710

Azalea Campground (Kings Canyon NP – Grant Grove)
- Season/elevation: Open year-round; 6,500 ft. Winters cold/snowy; summers warm/sunny with variable weather.
- Winter operations (Nov–Apr): Reduced to 20 sites (main loop only), first-come, first-served. Cashless payment via Recreation.gov mobile app (download beforehand; works offline).
- Summer reservations (May–Oct): All sites reservation-only; book up to 4 months in advance. For the 20 winter sites, reservations begin in early Jan; ≈90 additional sites open for reservations ~2 weeks later.
- Sites/vehicles: 110 total reservable sites (tent/RV). RVs up to 47 ft; trailers up to 30 ft. Paved, relatively flat roads.
- Fees: $32/night; $16/night with Senior/Access Pass. Winter fees paid via app QR.
- Water/toilets: Potable water year-round; flush toilets year-round.
- Accessibility: Site 30 is designated accessible (level surfaces, accessible parking, extended table, raised fire ring; flat paved road connects to fee station/restroom).
- Check times: Gates open/close at noon; check-in noon+; check-out before noon. Unchecked sites by noon on day 2 may be reassigned.
- Links: Info nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/azalea.htm; Reserve recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10124502

Buckeye Flat Campground (Sequoia NP)
