- Location/highlights: Generals Highway mile 6; near Middle Fork of the Kaweah River (audible from most sites). Paradise Creek Trail starts in campground; Middle Fork Trail nearby. Fire restrictions often in effect.
- Reservations: Normally all sites reservation-only up to 1 month in advance (currently paused).
- Sites/vehicles: 27 tent-only sites. No RVs/trailers.
- Fees: $32/night; $16/night with Senior/Access Pass.
- Water/toilets: Potable water seasonal; flush toilets (seasonal).
- Accessibility: Sites 20 and 24 designated accessible (features include extended picnic tables, food storage, raised fire rings/grills, level hard-packed tent pads, accessible parking; paved/level routes to facilities with some slopes).
- Links: Info nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/buckeye.htm; Reserve recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/249982

