Park-wide essentials
- Weather: Typically clear, <25% humidity. Spring/fall most comfortable (avg 85°F/50°F). Winter ~60°F days with freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations. Summer >100°F days, ~75°F nights. Weather can change quickly—check forecasts. Cottonwood area (3,000 ft) runs 5–10°F warmer than the park’s north.
- Regulations highlights: Pay camping fees within 1 hour of selecting/occupying a site (after-hours payment may be delayed to morning where noted). Check-in/out at noon. 30-day annual camping limit; only 14 nights allowed Oct–May. Set up tents/tarps/camping gear within 25 ft of the picnic table/fire grate. Store food and all scented items (incl. sunscreen/toiletries) securely from wildlife. Sites left vacant 24 hours may be treated as vacant. No holding sites for others. Pets leashed at all times; no unattended pets. No slacklines in campgrounds. Equestrian users: see park rules before visiting.
- Operating hours/quiet hours: Campgrounds open 24 hours daily; quiet hours 10 pm–6 am; check-in/out at noon.
- Contacts: 760-367-3001; jotr_info@nps.gov
- Camping regulations page: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/camping-regulations.htm

Belle Campground
- Size/type: 18 sites; first-come, first-served (FCFS) year-round.
- Facilities: Vault toilets; picnic tables; fire pits; no potable water—bring plenty.
- How to claim/pay: 1) Find an empty site, 2) Occupy it, 3) Proceed immediately to an entrance station to register and pay (within 1 hour; after-hours payment may be delayed to morning).
- Fees: $25/site; Senior/Access $12.50. Max per site: 6 people, 3 tents, 2 cars (some sites fit 1 vehicle).
- Accessibility/vehicles: No ADA sites; unpaved/uneven surfaces; paved/flat path to bathroom but unpaved road to path. RVs allowed up to 35 ft. Trailers not allowed. Unpaved access roads (all vehicles OK in good weather).
