Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'lavo', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 26233 tokens): Lassen Volcanic National Park – Camping and Backcountry Summary (key details)

Backcountry Camping in Lassen’s Wilderness (year-round)
- Overview: No designated sites or amenities; some areas closed to camping (near developed areas, bodies of water, hydrothermal areas). Winter camping allowed on/near the main park road when it’s closed due to snow.
- Permits: Required for all overnight stays outside established campgrounds; obtain online only at Recreation.gov before your trip (no mail/email/in-person). Carry a digital or printed copy.
- Group/Stay limits: Max group size 10; maximum stay 30 days per calendar year.
- Fees: $6 nonrefundable admin fee per permit + $5 per person per trip (no per-night fee). Reserve only one permit per trip.
- Regulations highlights: Bear-resistant containers required Apr 16–Nov 30; pets, bicycles, and overnight stock use not allowed; vehicles may be left in parking areas overnight per permit; catholes for human waste; pack out TP/hygiene products and all trash/food; firearms only with valid CA CCW; hunting prohibited; bear spray not permitted.
- Access/services: Primitive, no roads or services; no ADA facilities; OPDMDs not allowed in wilderness.
- Weather: Little precipitation July–Sept; up to 40 ft of winter snow; snow can linger into Jul/Aug; conditions vary with elevation—check forecasts.
- Info: Details/regulations: nps.gov/lavo/learn/management/backcountryregulations.htm; Permit: recreation.gov/permits/4675334; General info email: lavo_information@nps.gov

