- Fees (per night): Campsite $22; when water off $15; Group $62; Group (water off) $35; Stock corral $37.
- Sites: Total 101; all reservable; Group 6; Stock corral 1; no hookups.
- Amenities: Vault toilets (seasonal); potable water (seasonal); no showers; dump station; camp store; staff/host; bear lockers; trash/recycling.
- Regulations highlights: Pets leashed; drones prohibited; sites must be occupied upon payment; fees nonrefundable; max 14 days per year; checkout 12 pm; quiet hours 10 pm–6 am; generator hours 8–10 am, 12–2 pm, 5–7 pm; wash dishes at site; gather only small down wood near roads; no chainsaws; fires only in provided grates; fully extinguish.
- Accessibility/vehicles: ADA site A-6; RVs/trailers to 35 ft; unpaved access road (OK in good weather).
- Weather/elevation: 6,100 ft; highs ~68–84°F; lows ~29–39°F; usually snow-free by June.
- Info/booking: nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/butte-lake-campground.htm; recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234156; Phone 530-595-6121; Email lavo_fees@nps.gov

