2) Hike and Bike Day: Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway
- What: “Hike and Bike” Saturdays. The Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway (Prairie Creek Redwoods State Park) is closed to motorized vehicles the first Saturday of the month, October–May, so visitors can safely hike, bike, skate, and walk leashed pets along the 10-mile scenic drive.
- E-bikes: Allowed; speed limit 20 mph (typically Type 1 or Type 2). Violators creating unsafe conditions will be asked to leave; continued violations may lead to e-bikes being disallowed on future Hike and Bike days.
- Access: Prairie Creek Visitor Center and Elk Prairie Campground access is not affected. Use the southern entrance to the parkway (Exit 753). Parkway closes Friday afternoon and reopens Sunday morning after law enforcement assesses road conditions.
- Parking: Primary parking on the south end near Prairie Creek Visitor Center. Very limited parking and no facilities on the north end.
- Category: Regular Event
